  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-07-14T21:41:24.769Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Currently, in order to create multiple toggleable objects on an avatar, you have to use multiple animator parameters (limit of 16) since deactivating a button or toggle in the expression menu resets the value to 0.  If avatar creators were able to specify a 'reset value' for each button or toggle, they would be able to structure animator state machines to toggle on any number of objects without having to use more than one animator parameter.  \nAn example setup is shown using values 1 and 2 to toggle on two different objects, and values 255 and 254 for what would be distinguishable reset values to turn off each toggle.",
